body:
Is it possible you can disable this commit when autoRender is set to false, and not just debug off? This commit prevented me from upgrading to 2.6.0 and I had to rollback to 2.5.8 because I have ajax methods throughout my site that look like this:

``` php
public function getsomedata() {
    Configure::write('debug', 1);
    $this->autoRender = false;
    $data = $this->SomeModel->getSomeData('someparam');
    echo $data;
}
```

and plenty of others like this:

``` php
public function getsomedata2() {
    Configure::write('debug', 1);
    $this->autoRender = false;
    $data = $this->SomeModel->query("SELECT * FROM posts");
    echo json_encode($data);
}
```

Now I know with 2.6.0, if I use jsonViews for the 2nd method, problem solved, but I have hundreds of methods I would have to upgrade to jsonViews. The first method though, I don't know what is causing the headers to be already sent? And I don't know a way around it other than using `exit()` at the end.

I've been using CakePHP for my company since 2008, and my codebase has over 300,000 lines of code, and is difficult to maintain across upgrades with major changes like this that break my site. Sure as of 2.4 or whatever I should have started using jsonViews and what have you. But developers shouldn't be penalized for not using new features. Prior to that I had already implemented my own version of jsonViews, and the majority of my codebase is using it. But that causes this error on 2.6.0. Thank you for listening, sorry for the long post.

@pyrite357 I have different feelings about this. On the one hand, I understand your issue and that, even though you want to upgrade to the next minor release, you do not want to modify much code.

On the other hand, echoing (or outputting headers) directly in your controller never really was something you should have ever done in 2.x (not even in 2.0). And as such, asking for not breaking invalid code seems like a lot somehow, whereas you can either not (yet) upgrade to 2.6 or easily refactor your controller action code (as documented since 2.0):

``` php
    ...
    $this->autoRender = false;
    $data = $this->SomeModel->query("SELECT * FROM posts");
    $this->response->body(json_encode($data));
}
```

etc. Really minor changes.

Tip: try to automate it using preg_replace(), grapping `echo + ....` maybe.

Same thing, of course:

``` php
    ...
    $this->autoRender = false;
    $data = 'OK';
    $this->response->body($data);
}
```
